":"VRCE-4-12-18","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":12,"verse":18,"english":"The two brothers, exercised with ire, struck each other with palms like to Asani and with fists resembling adamant.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.941,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-12-18"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4012018","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"4ba1f0e8dba245ecb50bbf7d6236c3129c4a1947825cf852df24b48b966f2303","compact":"b6ffe6af47592cb9a25f694233333d65cc6d38f01d732dc552a6f3a94fb59bca","nasal":"b6ffe6af47592cb9a25f694233333d65cc6d38f01d732dc552a6f3a94fb59bca"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-12-19","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":12,"verse":19,"english":"Thereupon Rāma, with bow in hand, beheld those two heroes resembling each other, like to two Aświns.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.641,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-12-19"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4012019","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"a2d025c4fe0db9c67e4acedac511be801fb2ff3925b40f6e351da9c4b460562d","compact":"addfa73a333ea07adfacf774a2fbbb76e3292a65e5a80573f005e06afd29a729","nasal":"addfa73a333ea07adfacf774a2fbbb76e3292a65e5a80573f005e06afd29a729"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-12-20","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":12,"verse":20,"english":"And Rāghava did not discharge that mortal shaft until he could perfectly ascertain who was Vāli and who was Sugriva.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.889,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-12-20"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4012020","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"3028335e6edd6098fb57f759c20d40646b9a62e0adb76552d7411735f41cb349","compact":"fb1ab64bd26fc8d8e6b804335e7bcfc33f943daf83056cae5119d6afb220c16f","nasal":"dbed4c5444ee3